//! The variables Vim documents in the scopes `g:`, `b:`, `w:` and
//! `t:`. Vim or one of the plugins it ships reads or writes each one,
//! so a project that writes one writes it for a reader outside the
//! project, and one that reads one did not have to declare it.
//! REFERENCE: https://github.com/Galvarcus/GhostCode/issues/55
//!
//! Generated by `tools/vim-tables` from the `runtime/doc/tags` of
//! Vim 9.2. Never edited by hand: run the tool again against a
//! newer help directory.
//!
//! License: GNU GPL 3.0

